PATCH 367 -- the b059 BEARING/MOVEMENT cluster (objtype-0x02 crash-walk, master 0c7d4bc).  Two
near-offset/undefined2 base-losses on the a0ab->b059->a930->a19a->0927->0b71 proximity/range path,
asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00):

(1) FUN_0000_b059 (asm 0xb059) -- a0ab (asm 0xa112) passes param_3=SI, param_4=DI as DGROUP NEAR
    OFFSETS (both objects); b059's body + FUN_0000_b112(SI,DI) + FUN_1000_a930(...,SI,DI) deref them
    as host pointers -> the b112->0731 SIGSEGV (fault 0xca2e).  b112 has MIXED callers (35393/64636
    pass host ptrs) so the fix is at b059: rebase param_3/param_4 to g_mem+0x1c000+off once (patch-244
    idiom); the whole body + callee calls become correct verbatim.

(2) FUN_0000_a19a (asm 0xa19a = pure `call 0x927; lret` forwarder) -- its param_4/param_5 were typed
    undefined2 (uint16_t), so a930's call a19a(iVar2,p1,p2,&DAT_2000_5690,&DAT_2000_5684) TRUNCATED the
    two point-struct HOST pointers to 16 bits before 0927 (patch 328, takes int param_4/param_5 host
    ptrs) forwarded them to 0b71 -> host-ptr deref of a 16-bit stub (fault 0xa850; a930->a19a->0927->
    0b71).  Widened undefined2->int (fwd decl + def; the 328/330 class); param_1..3 stay (dead cx/dx/bx).

